  "clinical_evidence": [
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "It's my voice. It's... gone a bit. Rough, like. Since I was poorly in the winter, I've not, um...",
      "start_timestamp": "01:01",
      "end_timestamp": "01:10",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint",
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "A rough, hoarse voice since the winter illness. Cyril, has it come and gone, or is it the same every day?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:26",
      "end_timestamp": "01:38",
      "supports": [
        "symptoms[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "You're doing very well. Now, it's important I ask this because we may need to choose a medicine today. Do you have any allergies?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:15",
      "end_timestamp": "02:28",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Well, I... um, there's penicillin. I was told I'm allergic to it.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:29",
      "end_timestamp": "02:36",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "speaker_role": "family_member",
      "transcript_text": "He came out in a rash all over when he was given it, doctor. After a tooth abscess, I think, years ago. It's on his card but they never look.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:38",
      "end_timestamp": "02:54",
      "supports": [
        "allergies[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "I have asthma. Since I was a boy. And my blood pressure, it's a bit high, I'm told.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:28",
      "end_timestamp": "03:37",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Not really. My mother had thyroid problems, that's all I can think of.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:48",
      "end_timestamp": "03:54",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.family_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Thank you. A routine question I ask everyone with a voice change. Do you smoke, or have you ever?",
      "start_timestamp": "03:57",
      "end_timestamp": "04:08",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Never. Not once. I never smoked in my life. My father did, and I hated it.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:10",
      "end_timestamp": "04:18",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Rightly so. It makes some of the more worrying causes less likely. Now, let me take a couple of readings. Temperature is 36.6 degrees.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:33",
      "end_timestamp": "04:45",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And oxygen saturation is 97 percent, which is perfectly good for you.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:47",
      "end_timestamp": "04:53",
      "supports": [
        "vital_signs[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "The throat is a little red at the back, nothing alarming. Your voice has that husky, breathy quality, as Funmi said. Now let me feel your neck.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:28",
      "end_timestamp": "05:41",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Yes. There are no lumps in the neck on either side, and nothing tender. That's reassuring.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:54",
      "end_timestamp": "06:02",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'll explain my thinking. After a long illness with a lot of coughing, the voice box can get irritated and inflamed. Stomach acid creeping up at night can keep it irritated and slow the healing. From everything I've seen, that's the most likely explanation.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:13",
      "end_timestamp": "06:34",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "So I'd like to start you on a course of omeprazole, maybe 20 mg once a day, before breakfast. I'll confirm the exact strength when I write the prescription.",
      "start_timestamp": "06:53",
      "end_timestamp": "07:08",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]",
        "clinical_actions[0]",
        "clinical_uncertainties[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Most people notice nothing, though a mild headache or loose stools can happen. For the voice itself, give it rest, avoid whispering, which strains it more than speaking softly, and sip water through the day.",
      "start_timestamp": "07:17",
      "end_timestamp": "07:35",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I can see the family is in good hands. One last thing, and I want you both to hear it. If you ever have trouble breathing, noisy breathing, or difficulty swallowing, don't wait, call an ambulance.",
      "start_timestamp": "08:11",
      "end_timestamp": "08:29",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[2]"
      ]
    }
  ],
